Every clinician should assess a concurrent-substance-use.
If a state-PDMP-record is appropriate for a concurrent-substance-use-assessment then every clinician should use the state-PDMP-record during the concurrent-substance-use-assessment.
If a toxicology-testing is appropriate for a concurrent-substance-use-assessment then every clinician should use the toxicology-testing during the concurrent-substance-use-assessment.
If a patient has a concurrent-substance-use then the concurrent-substance-use can possibly increase an opioid-use-disorder-risk for the patient and can possibly increase an overdose-risk for the patient.
